251
00:13:54,380 --> 00:13:56,837
Oh, it came out of the wall.

252
00:13:56,920 --> 00:14:00,155
And now it's going back where
our guys can't get at it.

253
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:03,480
Very lethal.

254
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:04,997
They're cheating.

255
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:07,680
It moved too many spaces. On the contrary.

256
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:10,137
The wall shadow didn't move any spaces.

257
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:12,420
It moved on the wall. That's right.

258
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:14,756
And the wall doesn't have any spaces.

259
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:17,020
This is not good.

260
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:20,257
Our monsters have to count
spaces as they walk the maze,

261
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:23,217
while their wall shadow can
move through the maze walls.

262
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:26,418
And that means he can strike
when we least expect it.

263
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:34,380
So now you know our strategy is unleashing
a monster that you cannot see. You fools!

264
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:38,091
You won't know when the wall
shadow's about to land a blow.

265
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,900
We'll see about that.

266
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:42,300
Axe Raider in attack mode!

267
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:46,972
And I'll also place one other
card face down on the field.

268
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:54,417
But since I can't see your shifty
little monster, I can't attack it.

269
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:56,117
So I won't advance at all this turn.

270
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,477
I'll just keep Axe Raider as far away from

271
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:01,148
the wall and your Sneaky
Weasel as possible.

272
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:04,660
And I'll still be ready to
attack at any moment. Right?

273
00:15:05,220 --> 00:15:06,050
Right.

274
00:15:06,133 --> 00:15:07,257
That's a good move, Joey.

275
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:09,777
As long as you keep
far away from the wall,

276
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:12,697
you can avoid any sneak
attack by the wall shadow.

277
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:14,240
So far, so good.

278
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,500
I haven't cost us any life points.

279
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:17,750
Good move.

280
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,320
I hope Joey can keep this up.

281
00:15:19,980 --> 00:15:20,862
Don't sweat it.

282
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:23,377
With Yugi as his partner, Joey can't lose.

283
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:24,636
I hope you're right.

284
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,857
This tag team stuff is
tricky because they can

285
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:30,277
focus on attacking the
weakest duelists first.

286
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,190
You mean Joey.

287
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:32,510
My turn.

288
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,980
And I lay this card face down.

289
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:36,690
Jirai Gumo.

290
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:41,377
Any opposing monster that
steps on the space with Jirai

291
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:45,440
Gumo's symbol will instantly fall
victim to its fatal surprise.

292
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:52,420
I'll also lay the labyrinth tank in attack
mode and move it forward seven spaces.

293
00:15:58,820 --> 00:16:00,000
Good job, brother.

294
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:02,437
That should help trap
them within our maze.

295
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,620
Thank you, brother. It's my turn.

296
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:10,400
I play the Celtic Guardian in attack mode.

297
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:15,580
Advance four paces into the maze.

298
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:21,384
But the Celtic Guardian's attack strength
is much lower than that of Wall Shadows.

299
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:22,972
Then he'll be wiped out.

300
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,230
Ah!

301
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:27,610
You fool!

302
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,137
Did you not learn anything?

303
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:32,340
Wall Shadow, attack Celtic Guardian, no!

304
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:38,580
Your Guardian is doomed and
your life points with it!

305
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:46,140
Hm, I'm afraid not.

306
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,299
What do you mean, kunai with chain?

307
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,230
What is this?

308
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:52,060
My trap card worked!

309
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:54,740
Reel him in, Axe Raider!

310
00:16:57,520 --> 00:17:01,680
The card I played face down before
was a trap card, kunai with chain.

311
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:04,077
It captures any opponent that attacks.

312
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:06,137
I laid that trap card to help Yugi.

313
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:09,077
It raised the Celtic
Guardian's attack power by 500,

314
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:11,577
putting its strength
higher than Wall Shadows.

315
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:14,100
Celtic Guardian, attack Wall Shadow!

316
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:19,580
So now it's lights out
for your shadow. No!

317
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,940
Wall Shadow is beaten!

318
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:25,300
What a team!

319
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:28,837
Yeah, they're working together
to beat those wacky brothers.

320
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,357
Joey's really getting to
be a much better player.

321
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:33,087
He's thinking strategically.

322
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:34,050
Ah!

323
00:17:34,133 --> 00:17:36,417
To stop our decline,
these two we must halt!

324
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:37,500
Don't look at me!

325
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:38,740
It's not my fault!

326
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,500
If we keep this up,

327
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:43,977
we'll win this double duel and have
enough starships to enter the castle.

328
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:44,942
Teamwork, Yugi!

329
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:46,897
Right, but we haven't won yet.

330
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:48,537
We've got to keep on our guard.

331
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:51,357
if we're going to beat the
Paradox Brothers and win

332
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:54,680
our way out of this twisted
underground labyrinth.

333
00:17:55,020 --> 00:18:01,080
A toast to Yugi for winning the first round
with the help of his little pal, Joey.

334
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,100
Master Pegasus,

335
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:09,920
a thousand pardons for
interrupting your greatness.

336
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:13,592
I'm growing tired of your
constant interruptions, Croquet.

337
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:17,277
I thought you'd want to know Seto
Kaiba's been spotted on the island.

338
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:19,120
I already know that, Croquet.

339
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:23,851
Why are you, the head of my security,
always the last to learn these things?

340
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:24,790
Don't worry.

341
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,940
Kaiba will come to us after all.

342
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:29,000
We have the bait.

343
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:37,577
What's happened to you, brother?

344
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:38,895
Why haven't you come?

345
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,256
You said you'd always be here for me.

346
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:42,740
Well, where are you?

347
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,568
You never failed me before.

348
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:47,520
Give it back! Give it to me!

349
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,880
I give, I give!

350
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:53,780
Here, Mokuba. Thanks.

351
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,560
You always come through for me.

352
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:02,740
So where are you now, Seto?

353
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:04,560
Why haven't you found me?

354
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:05,880
I need you!

355
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:08,022
Why haven't you stopped Pegasus?

356
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:14,820
I'm coming, Mokuba.

357
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:16,493
I'm coming to save you.

358
00:19:16,620 --> 00:19:20,760
And if Pegasus tries to get in
my way, he'll live to regret it.
